nodecode-hardlight is a rewrite of nosliwhtes's nosliwhtes/hardlight-ui:

  https://github.com/nosliwhtes/hardlight-ui
  commit 2254efe3ba6df2fa5962cd8ed352b5fad80306d4
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 Seth Wilson and Hardlight UI contributors (LICENSE)

The original is a Hermes Agent plugin: five stateless tools (hardlight_reference,
hardlight_direction, hardlight_inspect, hardlight_contrast, hardlight_navigation), one
skill (skills/frontend-design/SKILL.md) and a /hardlight command. What is rewritten here
is the same five tools and the same command in one Common Lisp cell, against Nodecode's
own declarations: the reference topics, the exact style IDs, the WCAG thresholds, the
surface defaults, the direction packet's worksheet and verification matrix, the graph
analysis with its limits and the bounded walk are all the original's, in the original's
words where the words are the substance. The guides and the two data files ride with the
cell under data/, unchanged. The skill is the cell's manual, (help :hardlight), and its
one line rides every request.

What is left out, and why: the optional local-browser runner (hardlight/browser.py), which
needs Playwright and an already installed browser to capture a page, is not carried -- it
is a CLI-only extra, the cell runs no browser, and the answers state the same limitation;
the JSON CLI (hardlight/cli.py) is covered by the five tools and /hardlight; the HTML
findings come from a tag scan rather than Python's HTMLParser, so a malformed tag is
matched by shape rather than parsed; and the walk resolves the root and skips symbolic
links by comparing true names, where the original opens every ancestor with O_NOFOLLOW.
Nothing of the Python package, and no Node, Python or original source, is carried.
